Subject: Connecting LAN via RAS dialup to a Decserver 700
Date: 1997/04/12
Message-ID: <01bc4797$ceb58e50$99af82cc@nexus>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 234421328
Newsgroups: biz.dec.ip,comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec,comp.sys.vms,vmsnet.misc,vmsnet.networks.desktop.misc,vmsnet.networks.management.misc,vmsnet.networks.tcp-ip.misc,vmsnet.networks.tcp-ip.ucx,vmsnet.networks.tcp-ip.wintcp


	We've had good success for some time using Windows 3.1, Win95,
WinNT to make RAS connections to a corporate Decserver for single
computers using PPP.  Now trying to connect a LAN this way.  I have
the NT RAS client correctly routing traffic over the dialup, as
evidenced by RAS transmission activity when a node on the dialup
LAN attempts to ping the Decserver.  But Decserver activity for
all but the RAS client are never routed back over the phone line.
In Q121877 Microsoft says "You must set up a static route on the
third-party PPP or SLIP server (the Decserver) that routes traffic
destined for the RAS clients local LAN through the RAS IP address
of the RAS client."  This piece I am sure is missing.  But that is
because I don't know how to tell a Decserver to do this.  Any
ideas?

TIA - Lee

