   I have a single VAXstation 4000-96 on at the end of our Intranet and Decnet
   is not routed at this location ( and I can't get them to route it ).  The 
   local VAX network I am trying to reach runs Both Decnet and TCP/IP.  I have
   heard that you can route Decnet over the TCP/IP but have not been able to
   find out how ?  The application I am running requires decnet communication.
   I am running VAX/VMS 5.5-2 and the UCX is version 4.1.   Can anyone out
   there lend a hand in pointing me in the right direction ?

DECnet/OSI or DECnet-Plus, whichever name is the most correct this week.
The problem is that you need to upgrade VMS.  I can't recall that there
would be a DECnet-Plus for VMS 5.5, but I may be wrong...

Another solution is to change your TCP/IP stack.  MultiNet supports DECnet
over TCP/IP, see http://www.cisco.com/warp/public/751/multinet/movms_ds.htm


